# Write clear summaries

A summary is the line under a title: helper text on a card, a hint under a field, the preview of a notification. It should tell someone in one line whether this is the right place.

## Add something the title does not say

Do not repeat the title. Start with a verb. End with a full stop. Keep the main point in the first 160 characters.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Living room lights. This card shows the living room lights. | 2 of 4 lights on. |
| Schedule. A schedule. | Choose when the heating comes on each day. |
| Notification. You have a notification. | Front door opened at 22:15. |

Do not say what type of thing it is (“this card shows…”).

<h2 id="wg-053">Put help beside the decision</h2>

Place a hint where the person is deciding. Do not send them to another page to understand a field.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Duration (see the help centre for details) | Duration<br>How long the light stays on after movement. For example, 5 minutes. |

<h2 id="wg-055">Support learning without overloading the task</h2>

Give the one fact needed now. Offer more as a clearly named option, not as extra text in the way.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Zigbee is a low-power mesh protocol that uses 2.4GHz, supports up to hundreds of nodes and routes through mains-powered devices to extend range… | Zigbee devices pass messages through each other. Plug in a mains-powered Zigbee device between the hub and the sensor. A details section titled “How Zigbee routing works”. |

<h2 id="wg-056">Keep examples honest</h2>

A hint may give an example. Say it is an example and make sure it works in this household.

| Before | After |
| --- | --- |
| Example: light.bedroom | For example, `light.reading_lamp`. This is an example only. Use the ID of your own light. |
